You made an excellent observation. Because we changed the backend architecture to use the Draft (S) state, the batch isn't *actually* submitted to the Checkers until Step 3.
Currently, the final button just says "Execution routing finalized successfully!", which doesn't sound like a true submission. Furthermore, the buttons in your Excel Bulk Upload file still say "Validate & Submit", which is now misleading since it only prepares the draft!
Let's fix the terminology across the board so the user understands exactly when the batch is officially submitted.
### 1. Update the Final Success Message (VoucherPosting.jsx)
When the user clicks the final "Submit" button on Step 3, we should show them the official success message with their Batch ID.
**Find this inside handleFinalizeRouting (around line 235):**
```javascript
       await callApi("/JS/voucher/update-schedule", {
        batchId: submittedBatchId,
        scheduledTime: formattedSchedule 
      }, "POST");

      showSnackBar("Execution routing finalized successfully!", "success");
      handleResetWizard();

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
      await callApi("/JS/voucher/update-schedule", {
        batchId: submittedBatchId,
        scheduledTime: formattedSchedule 
      }, "POST");

      // SHOWS THE OFFICIAL SUBMISSION MESSAGE HERE
      showSnackBar(`Success! Batch ID ${submittedBatchId} has been successfully submitted for approval.`, "success");
      handleResetWizard();

```
*(Also, as a quick bonus fix: Scroll down to line 1251 in your <TimePicker> and change minTime={dayjs().add(30, 'minute')} to **31** so it matches the text below it!)*
### 2. Fix the Wording in Excel Upload (VoucherBulkUpload.jsx)
Because the Excel file now creates a Draft and pushes the user to Step 3, we need to remove the word "Submit" from the intermediate steps so the user isn't confused.
Open your **VoucherBulkUpload.jsx** file and make these two quick text changes near the bottom of the file:
**Find the Success Alert (around line 305 in BulkUpload):**
```javascript
          {batchCreated && (
            <Alert severity="success" sx={jbuStyles.successAlert}>
              <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="bold">Batch Successfully Validated and Submitted!</Typography>

```
**Change it to:**
```javascript
          {batchCreated && (
            <Alert severity="success" sx={jbuStyles.successAlert}>
              <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="bold">Batch Successfully Validated and Prepared!</Typography>

```
**Find the Upload Button at the very bottom (around line 324 in BulkUpload):**
```javascript
                <Button
                  variant="contained"
                  size="large"
                  onClick={handleStartValidation}
